verdict=IN-SCOPE: Plan item 1c's added paragraph (after "Committed as 551f373") explicitly prescribes this exact fix — "the arm sets Sky colour smoothing to 0 after the look, a second 'Internal:' commit to the walk, and the fail-first is run again" — because the look's smoothing-map rebuild differs by up to 6 levels/255 (measured, cause not established), which the byte-for-byte pick check misreads as the mask moving the photograph. The diff adds precisely this: an `after: { skySmooth: "0" }` field on the sky-band arm, applied via a new `setValue`-driven loop right after the look is applied (before the bare-view read), plus the corresponding `setValue` import — confined to tools/agreement-walk.mjs.
